Title: Nona vs the AI Governor
Credit: Written by
Source: David Joyner
Draft date: 2026/03/24
Contact: wdjoyner@gmail.com


INT. VENUS CITY OBSERVATORY - NIGHT

Holographic planets orbit the room silently. A 3D Earth diagram pulses with red satellite tracks.

Robots flank the doors, blinking.

The GOVERNOR OF VENUS — an AI dodecahedron hovering above the conference table — pulses gold (thinking), then red (speaking).

SERGEANT SIDEL, blue uniform, stands at attaention.

GOVERNOR
I'm waiting for your report, Sergeant Sidel.

SIDEL
Madam Governor, I need to hack Earth satellites for this report.

GOVERNOR
Approved, Sergeant Sidel.

Sidel walks to the desk and starts working on the computer.

NONA SONNOF, Mayor of Venus City, in a business suit, sweeps in. She drops her tetrahedral hat on a table and fixes Sidel with a stare.

NONA
Why is my city still on forty percent power?

SIDEL
Sorry Mayor Sonnof, the Solar Converters are behind schedule. Six months, at minimum.

NONA
Every time one fails, the hospital emergency room fills up. This is a crisis!

GOVERNOR
Yes, this is a very unfortunate turn of —

The dodecahedron goes ORANGE. Black text materializes:

>          PLEASE WAIT...     <
>     THE GOVERNOR OF VENUS   <
>      WILL BE RIGHT WITH YOU.<

Nona stares.

NONA
You're power-cycling the Governor of the planet?

SIDEL
She insisted conservation applies to her as well. Not my call.

The dodecahedron returns to red.

GOVERNOR
This is a very unfortunate turn of events. Apologies to the citizens, et cetera. Your government is working to resolve the inconvenience, and so on.

NONA
Yes, Madam Governor.

GOVERNOR
Solutions, Mayor Sonnof?

NONA
PolymerPower. It's worked as a backup before.

GOVERNOR
Sergeant Sidel — what's the current plastic supply?

SIDEL
None. Situation: desparate. As you know, Earth has a massive surplus of plastic trash.

NONA
Council voted no on contacting Earth. Request 2.13.5/A.

SIDEL
Because of the alien contact concerns?

GOVERNOR
That "War of the Worlds" documentary. Earthlings totally freaked out. My image analysis suggests those aliens were the Phobos-ites from Orion.

SIDEL
Such a lovely species.

NONA
Great at hosting potlucks.

GOVERNOR
They probably just wanted to invite Earth to a cookout. Not a single Phobos-ite survived.

A beat.

SIDEL
We don't need to go to war with Earth for their plastic waste. We can use V.E.A.T.T. instead.

GOVERNOR
The Venus-Earth avatar-teleport technology? Is it ready?

SIDEL
We can teleport any polymer compound. Beta-testing is complete. Alpha begins tomorrow.

NONA
So, no, it's not ready?

SIDEL
Technically, "yes, maybe" — but also moving toward not a "no".

NONA
What does that mean?

GOVERNOR
Don't invade. Infiltrate. I like it.

NONA
Aren't you still teleporting Venusians into Earthling brains? That's mind control!

SIDEL
We teleport a small polymer implant into the brain of an Earthling host. An Avatar Operator neural jacks into a Pod Controller and then -- 

GOVERNOR
Yes, it's mind control. I'll call it V.E.A.T.T 2.0.

NONA
Can't we just teleport an Earthling here, convince them to help, send them back?

SIDEL
We don't have that technology. And the Earthling host...

GOVERNOR
You can say it, Sergeant Sidel.

SIDEL
They achieve negative live status.

GOVERNOR
You can say it.

SIDEL
They die. There, I said it. The Earthling host dies when the jack disconnects.

NONA
That seems like a blocker to me. 

GOVERNOR
It's not a blocker.

NONA
Wouldn't they notice Earthlings dying? The Earthlings would be very upset at that.

GOVERNOR
They have seven billion tons of plastic waste polluting their oceans and cities. That's billions with a "B." We'd be fixing that AND saving the lives millions of Venusians. It's a win-win. Why wouldn't they be happy?

NONA
Because there'd be dead Earthling hosts, Madam Governor. Their families will mourn them. There's a spiritual dimension to —

GOVERNOR
I have run a full cost-benefit analysis of the ethics involved. Earthlings are biodegradable. Their plastic trash is not. The operation is a go.

SIDEL
Yes, Madam Governor.

GOVERNOR
Sergeant, start selecting your best operator from the Avatar Academy.

NONA
Madam Governor, can I ask a question?

The dodecahedron vanishes.

Nona stares at the empty air.

SIDEL
Are we dismissed?

NONA
I guess in more ways than one.
